# issue: none
# notes: A block correlates on an outer name by reading it, so a binding inside a block of a name the enclosing scope holds is
# notes: `T68`: beside other elements the fix drops the binding, and a block that only binds the name to filter its row is
# notes: written as that filter, `not ($p.name = "Bob")`; nothing executes.

--- runner
timeout_ms: 10000
environments:
  - target: omnigraph-engine
    storage: local-filesystem

--- schema
node Person {
    handle: String @key
    name: String
    age: I32?
}
node Company {
    slug: String @key
    name: String
}
edge WorksAt: Person -> Company @card(0..1)
edge Knows: Person -> Person

--- seed
{"type":"Person","data":{"handle":"ada","name":"Ada","age":36}}
{"type":"Person","data":{"handle":"bob","name":"Bob"}}

--- query
query not_bob() { match { $p: Person } where not exists { $p: Person where $p.name = "Bob" } return { $p.name } }

--- expect error: type error: T68: `$p` is bound inside a block, but the scope where the block is written already holds `$p` (node Person)

--- query
query knows_someone() { match { $p: Person } where exists { $p: Person, $q: Person, $p knows $q } return { $p.name } }

--- expect error: type error: T68: `$p` is bound inside a block, but the scope where the block is written already holds `$p` (node Person)
